Z||000007||Posthumane||12-18-2001||08:18 PM||||I just went to a rally cross this sunday and one about a month ago. Had a blast, but I cracked part of my air dam on sunday (84 SE - very small air dam), so I'm going to make a better one out of fiberglass, or atleast try. The problem with the fiero in rallying is it REALLY understeers on loose surfaces when trying to turn into a tight corner. The only way to get around is to forcibly break the back end loose (turn in, stab brakes, throw up one gear, rev it and dump clutch).<P>Rocky mnt. Rally a few years back:   <IMG SRC="http://www.bishop.ab.ca/CSCC/Photos/FIERO.gif">  <P><p>[This message has been edited by Posthumane (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
