Z||000009||Master_Sushi||12-19-2001||12:07 AM||||I've strangely ended up off the road a few times in my fieros  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">... I won't normally drive my fiero offroad though. I might try it some time for fun though. Rear engine VWs were pretty good offroad because of the extra weight over the drive tires. I would think that fieros would do ok because of this same fact. I didn't get stuck once with my 88 coupe in the winter.||||reg||10
Z||000010||BlackStang95||12-19-2001||02:09 AM||||With mods it might make a dandy rally racer, but stock it would break parts.  But for real "off-roading" you need a jeep or modded bronco/blazer.||||reg||1
Z||000011||falconhulk||12-19-2001||12:39 PM||||BS Ralleying is not the same as 4x4 offroading.  4x4 offroading is about what obsicles can I take and still not bust my truck up.  Rally races are about how fast can i go on gravel without wiping out on the next sharp left mud filled turn.  Its a totally diffrent experiance then a 4x4.||||reg||1
